7. THIRD-PARTY APIS, BYOM ARCHITECTURE & PRIVACY GUARANTEE
================================================================================

7.1. Bring-Your-Own-Model (BYOM) Independence:
     NativeLingo is built as an independent client interface and local assistant. 
     The Software connects directly to third-party language model providers 
     (such as Google Gemini, OpenAI-compatible APIs) or local offline inference 
     servers (such as Ollama or LM Studio) designated by the Licensee.

7.2. End User API Obligations:
     Licensee acknowledges that access to third-party cloud AI APIs may require 
     separate API keys, accounts, and fee arrangements directly with such providers. 
     Licensor does not provide, resell, or guarantee third-party cloud API services, 
     token quotas, or service availability.

7.3. Privacy and Local Data Confidentiality:
     NativeLingo contains zero built-in behavioral tracking, zero background telemetry, 
     and zero cloud intermediary proxy servers. When operating in local BYOM mode 
     (e.g., via Ollama or LM Studio), 100% of text processing and translation remains 
     strictly confined to the Licensee's local hardware memory. Licensor never has 
     access to, collects, inspects, or stores Licensee's clipboard content, prompts, 
     or translation outputs.

